SUMMARY:TEC Seminar: Ori Heffetz\, Cornell University - Explaining Mechan
 isms: Experts Make A Difference
LOCATION:North Hall 2111
DESCRIPTION:Speaker: Ori Heffetz\, Cornell University\nTitle: "Explaining
  Mechanisms: Experts Make A Difference"\nHosted by: Jason Somerville\n\n
 We asked expert market designers to explain the Vickrey-Clarke-Groves au
 ction to lab participants. We randomized the explanation provided\, and 
 then measured bidding behavior\, understanding\, and self-reported attit
 udes. We compared experts to two benchmarks: an explanation generated by
  an AI model\, and a control treatment that simply asserts that straight
 forward bidding maximizes profits\n\nhttps://econ.ucsb.edu/events/all/20
 26/tec-seminar-ori-heffetz-cornell-university
URL:https://econ.ucsb.edu/events/all/2026/tec-seminar-ori-heffetz-cornell
 -university
CATEGORIES:TEC
SEQUENCE:3
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
