SUMMARY:TEC Seminar: Ruru Hoong\, MIT Sloan
LOCATION:North Hall 2111
DESCRIPTION:Speaker: Ruru Hoong\, MIT Sloan\nHosted by: Jason Somerville\
 n\nRuru Hoong is an Assistant Professor of Marketing at the MIT Sloan Sc
 hool of Management. Her research examines how organizations should desig
 n and integrate new digital technologies\, particularly artificial intel
 ligence\, into decision-making. She asks not only whether AI improves de
 cisions\, but who benefits\, on which tasks\, and under what organizatio
 nal conditions---highlighting why the same technology can generate sharp
 ly uneven gains across people\, tasks\, and firms. Hoong also studies ho
 w digital technologies shape consumer behavior and welfare. Her research
  examines how platform and product design affect self-control\, engageme
 nt\, and wellbeing\; how consumers choose among and develop preferences 
 for new technologies\; and how technological change reshapes what people
  value more broadly. Across these areas\, she combines economic theory w
 ith field experiments\, large-scale data\, and quantitative methods to u
 nderstand how technologies can be designed and deployed to improve decis
 ion quality\, organizational performance\, and longer-run wellbeing. Hoo
 ng’s research has received several honors\, including the David A. Wel
 ls Prize for Best Dissertation from Harvard University in 2026\, the Vit
 hala Rao Best PhD Paper Award at the 2026 AI in Management Conference\, 
 an Exemplary Paper Award at the 2026 ACM Conference on Economics and Com
 putation (EC ’26)\, and Best Conference Paper\, Runner-Up\, at the 202
 5 Conference on Information Systems and Technology (CIST). She graduated
  from Stanford in\n\nhttps://econ.ucsb.edu/events/all/2027/tec-seminar-r
 uru-hoong-mit-sloan
URL:https://econ.ucsb.edu/events/all/2027/tec-seminar-ruru-hoong-mit-sloa
 n
CATEGORIES:TEC
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
